1
00:00:04,194 --> 00:00:11,017
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

2
00:00:11,017 --> 00:00:13,017
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

3
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:14,960
Needy...

4
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,980
I know it is trying to offer us something great,

5
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,240
but what IS that speaker thing?

6
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,960
I suggest we dismantle it to find out!

7
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,140
Hyup!

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,140
Uh-oh, I missed.

9
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,520
Leafy! What's happened?

10
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:30,520
You've become EVIL!

11
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,880
Icy!

12
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,480
Icy, I'm sorry I killed you.

13
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,880
I want revenge!

14
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:40,040
Cake at Stake.

15
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:41,020
♪ Da-da-da-da-da-da ♪

16
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,700
♪ Cake at Stake! ♪

17
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:47,000
So, since the Cherries were dumber,
they got a lower total test score.

18
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,300
One of them goes home.

19
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,020
And the number of votes is...

20
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:54,940
Hold on 1/60th of a minute.
That doesn't seem right.

21
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:57,540
Oink, there it is.

22
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,840
It was the second time that digit was used,

23
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:01,980
and the third time that digit was used.

24
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,900
We weren't sure if they would work.

25
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,860
Oh, and, um, Cherries, uh, well,

26
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:09,760
I forgot to buy a cake, so I had to make something.

27
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,260
It's a [BAM] sliced chunk of ice.

28
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:13,500
MMMPH.

29
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:17,260
So yeah, if you remain
ice-chunk-less, you leave BFDI.

30
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,880
And Ice Cube, what are you doing here?

31
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,100
You're on the other team.

32
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:22,280
ICE CUBE:
AAAAAH!

33
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,080
Moving on...

34
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:26,140
Pin, you have a Win Token.
Would you like to use it now?

35
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,320
Uh, no.

36
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,100
I mean, there's nothing mean I-

37
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,640
Yeah, yeah. We know.

38
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,800
Anyway, at zero votes, it's-

39
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,320
It's got to be Block-

40
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:35,680
No. It's not.

41
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:37,060
It's all girls...

42
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:37,700
GIRLS:
Yeah!

43
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:38,680
...except Match...

44
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:39,880
- MATCH: Hey! Hey!
- PIN: Yeah!

45
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,660
...and Pin.

46
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:41,720
- MATCH: Yeah!
- PIN: Hey!

47
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:42,320
Yeah.

48
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,660
AAAAAHHHHH!

49
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,660
Firey, Eraser, and Pen...

50
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:49,740
also no votes.

51
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:50,700
Woo!

52
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,580
ERASER & PEN:
AAAAAHHHHH!

53
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,580
Yeah, elbow room!

54
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:00,680
ANNOUNCER:
Match and Pin, you only got one vote a piece.

55
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,960
A piece? A PIECE?!

56
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,800
You know, we aren't just objects!

57
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,729
- Well, maybe Pin is.

58
00:02:05,729 --> 00:02:06,040
- PIN: Hey!
- Well, maybe Pin is.

59
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,080
We have feelings, too!

60
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:07,854
- But Pin's don't matter.

61
00:02:07,854 --> 00:02:08,380
- PIN: Hey!
- But Pin's don't matter.

62
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:08,740
- Yeah!

63
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:09,240
- PIN: Hey!
- Yeah!

64
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,360
Match! Are you okay?

65
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,360
Hey, how are you back?

66
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,880
I thought you flew away.

67
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,480
Off beyond the horizon!

68
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:21,480
You're seeing strange things
because you're HALLUCINATING!

69
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,440
See? I'll turn into DUMB Bubble!

70
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,020
Buh!

71
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:26,920
Don't do that!

72
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,060
It is K-R-E-P!

73
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,480
Dun-dun!

74
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:31,140
Blocky-

75
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:33,140
HEAAAUUUGHUEAAAOOOH!

76
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:34,840
-is eliminated at six votes.

77
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,680
Ahh...

78
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,040
Whoa, déjà vu!

79
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:39,140
Blocky gone?

80
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,920
But that can't be!

81
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,920
Blocky's a great guy!

82
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,760
He's my friend, too!

83
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,200
And he's only killed two people.

84
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,220
Yeah, whatever.

85
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:54,040
BLOCKY:
AAAAAAAAAH!

86
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,140
ANNOUNCER:
And, with that, the Squashy Grapes,

87
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:59,120
the original losers, are now ahead at nine to eight.

88
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,640
And Golf Ball's chance of winning went from...

89
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:04,140
GOLF BALL:
...5.555 repeating percent

90
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:06,420
to 5.882 percent!

91
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,860
Phoo! Yuck! That was terrible!

92
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:11,280
Well, let's see if you can do any better.

93
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:15,260
Because the next challenge is all
about food, cooking it, and eating it.

94
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,600
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

95
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,160
Wait, we already played that, didn't we?

96
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,980
Okay, so the remaining seventeen
of you will each bake a cake.

97
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,440
I'll be one judge. Let's see.

98
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:29,280
Flower, a previously-eliminated
contestant, could be our second.

99
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,320
And the magical die of judgment-

100
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,500
-will be our third.

101
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:36,280
Wait. Is that just a normal die?

102
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,380
Um, maybe.

103
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:40,540
So yeah. Your scores will be out of twenty-six.

104
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,600
Here are some ingredients.

105
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:47,300
There are no recipes for you to follow,
and you may use any flavors you like.

106
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:50,660
The contestant that makes the
best cake receives a Win Token.

107
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:53,080
Look! It's Bubble

108
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:56,340
Remember? How she can't count to three?

109
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:58,600
Oh, yeah, she's really dumb.

110
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,700
Guys, I'm not dumb.

111
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,120
I just died before I could get to three!

112
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,700
See? I can do it!

113
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,040
One, two...

114
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:09,580
Yeah, she's really dumb. Dumb for sure!

115
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:12,900
Mix, mix, mix, mix, mix, mix!

116
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,600
No recipes?

117
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:17,720
How are you supposed to
make a cake without recipes?

118
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:21,020
It's as bad as making a cake out of DIRT!

119
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:24,540
Oh! Uh, well...

120
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:27,500
a DIRT cake is stil
better than an ICE cake.

121
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:31,500
TENNIS BALL:
Look, GB! I finished!

122
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,060
It's a rice cake.

123
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,100
Um... hey, Leafy!

124
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:37,740
Why are you making such a big cake?

125
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:42,460
So if anyone is having trouble making
a cake themselves, I can lend some!

126
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,640
Oh, so is it like you do it for me?

127
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,220
Um, I guess?

128
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:51,060
Good news, Pen! Leafy is
going to make our cakes!

129
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,600
Well, that's not what I was planning for.

130
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,600
So there's a price to pay!

131
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:58,680
Wha-oops! There's the jar I was looking for!

132
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,820
Pay up, boys! Minimum tip is five dollars!

133
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,960
Oh. I don't have any money.

134
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,380
- Pen, you got some?

135
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:06,100
- Hmm...
- Pen, you got some?

136
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,060
Here!

137
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:08,840
I have eight dollars!

138
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:10,040
That'll be enough!

139
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:10,560
Grr!

140
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,040
Baking cakes without recipes

141
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:15,200
is as almost as bad as making a cake out of

142
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,580
TWO METAL BALLS!

143
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:32,740
I know, but eight dollars will only
get you one cake, dum-dums!

144
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,780
Hey! I see something!

145
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,780
Awh, we're still one cent short!

146
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,640
Coiny's a penny, right?

147
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,160
PEN:
Yeah!

148
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,560
Well, I'll get ten points from Flower, right?

149
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,920
One, two, three!

150
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,660
Four, five, six, seven, eight!

151
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,120
Hey, Match?

152
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,940
Maybe Bubble ISN'T dumb!

153
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:51,940
La, la!

154
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,180
Cake's done!

155
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:53,780
[SNIFF]

156
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:55,460
It smells... DIRTY!

157
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:57,660
Oh, well. Probably just me.

158
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,280
Now my cake is done!

159
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,940
Heh, heh! Need an oven, Coiny?

160
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:05,520
Not me. I'M my oven!

161
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:06,680
Huh?

162
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,040
COINY:
Hey, put me down!

163
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,040
Hah, hah!

164
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,020
Bleh!

165
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,400
Thirty minutes left.

166
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,400
Uh-oh, we haven't started!

167
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:18,360
I have twenty bucks. Let's buy some of Leafy's cakes!

168
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:20,600
Woody?

169
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,080
Do you need help?

170
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,220
I'll lend you a cake for FREE!

171
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:26,120
FOR FREE?!

172
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:26,960
Well, um...

173
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,800
Leafy, we need three cakes.

174
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,260
Here's fifteen dollars.

175
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,760
And give these five to Woody.

176
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,860
Well, I guess it ALL WORKS OUT!

177
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:41,900
Since Ice Cube is non-existent
at the moment, she is excused.

178
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,900
Let's go in alphabetical order.

179
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:45,440
So Bubble is up.

180
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,440
Good luck, not-dumb friend!

181
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,200
Hmm, normal strawberry cake.

182
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,260
Taste test.

183
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,140
Hmm, pretty good. Eight out of ten.

184
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:59,840
Right now, I'm really angry because I got voted off!

185
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:00,720
GRR!

186
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:04,080
Hey! That cake looks terrible!

187
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,080
Zero out of ten! Well...

188
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,860
one out of ten because I'm just SO nice.

189
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:10,060
And the die.

190
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:13,920
Coiny's turn.

191
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:16,260
It's, uh... baked dirt!

192
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:19,140
Um, well, dirt is unsafe, so I won't eat it.

193
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,460
I'm sorry, but dirt will get a two.

194
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:24,680
Well, a DIRT cake is better than an ICE cake.

195
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,880
Which rhymes with rice cake!

196
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:27,820
Flower?

197
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:32,260
Well, I see you put effort
into it, like baking it and stuff.

198
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:36,020
I'll give it a seven for what
wonderful things it could have been!

199
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,520
OMBB!

200
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:42,220
Dirt got a better score than mine?!

201
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:45,480
It's okay! You just bake at a sub-dirt level!

202
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,320
Eraser.

203
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:49,280
Strawberry again? Same as Bubble?

204
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:52,280
I'll give it a seven this time, because it's the same.

205
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,820
Hmm. Ten?

206
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:54,840
YEAH!

207
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,440
Awh!

208
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,420
Firey.

209
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,940
Mine's chocolate!

210
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:01,480
You baked without the oven?

211
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,840
That's an automatic ten for effort!

212
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,200
I wouldn't say so!

213
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,600
I pick THREE!

214
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,080
And the die picks six.

215
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,480
Golf Ball?

216
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,140
Hey! I taste dirt!

217
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:15,140
But I didn't put in any dirt!

218
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:17,440
Putting in dirt and lying? I say zero!

219
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,640
I will, too!

220
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:19,920
And so does the die.

221
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,340
Wait! A die doesn't even have-

222
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:21,840
Shush!

223
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,040
Ice Cube is gone, so Leafy is up next.

224
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:28,700
Strawberry again?
This is starting to get irritating.

225
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:30,060
So you get a four.

226
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:31,760
But I was the first to make the-

227
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,460
Quiet, weightless one! I have my answer.

228
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,060
Wait, not yet.

229
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,180
LEAFY:
Yes!

230
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:39,900
I choose ZERO!

231
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:40,600
Wha-?

232
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,520
Die.

233
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,600
WOW! The die says fifteen!

234
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,420
Okay, we are done. Let's compare.

235
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:55,640
I guess since Pin has the highest score with her
Flower Cake, she gets her second Win Token.

236
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:59,300
Note, Pin, that you can only
use one Win Token at a time.

237
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:03,180
Okay, now let's organize by team to see who won.

238
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,960
So I guess the Cherries win this half of the contest.

239
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:11,100
In the second half, each team will
eat a hundred chocolate balls.

240
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,260
The fastest team wins.

241
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,520
And start eating.

242
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:19,020
EVERYONE:
OM NOM NOM!

243
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:22,680
ANNOUNCER:
Well, the Grapes won this part, so now it's a two-way tie.

244
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:24,500
So we need a tie breaker.

245
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:28,840
Whichever team manages to rip their
team necktie first wins the contest.

246
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,800
Get it? Tie breaker?

247
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:35,660
The Squashy Grapes win, so
one of the Cherries goes home.

248
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:39,480
Come on, choose one. You know you want to.

249
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,580
Breaking news!

250
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:49,160
Scientists have recently classified
Earth as a triple planet system!

251
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:52,880
Consisting of Earth, the Moon and
something called 'Needle's Cake'.

252
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:56,820
That is supposedly a rapidly-growing cake
that has separated from Earth.

253
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:59,860
Scientists predict that Needle's
Cake will start nuclear fusion

254
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:02,060
and become a star in three weeks.

255
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:05,540
Yeah, I guess it's pretty big, Needy.